HST Office: the ribbon banner always shows its wide artwork; a collapsed group shows its icon.

Owner decision (13/11/2026): the HASON TECH banner is shown at every window width, including 1366 px; it
never hides and never switches to the compact artwork. It only narrows, keeping its ratio, down to
MIN_WIDE_ART_WIDTH (260 logical px), the width at which its logo, title, text, link and "HASON TECH" stay
legible, and that width stays reserved: when the groups do not fit beside it, they collapse by priority
into their "Caption ▾" buttons (fitByPriority, hst-ribbon-ux-engine.patch).
- NotebookbarTabControl: a two-row tab page always gets the wide banner (a one-row ribbon none); the
  window-width threshold that showed the compact artwork below 1280 px no longer applies.
- PriorityMergedHBox: a collapsed group's button shows the large icon of the group's first command
  (toolbox item or drop-down button; the caption's dialog launcher does not count) above "Caption ▾",
  as Office does, instead of bare text.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: build only (both files syntax-checked against the configured tree). Runtime: every app and tab at
1366, 1440, 1485, 1536, 1600 and 1920 px shows the wide banner (260 to 360 px), and a collapsed group shows
an icon above its caption.
